post-mutation restored build: GREEN

Survivor analysis. words_seal_not_persisted stops persistence.cpp from writing
the Word-of-Power bit 0x80 into GAM 0x32a. W9 (save, power cycle, load) stayed
GREEN because the sidecar's gameState.questFlags also carries word-spoken:33 and
load_native_state takes the sidecar's questFlags. The device's own reload was
therefore fine, but the GAM it wrote no longer matched the original format. The
test gained W7b (the saved GAM's 0x32a bit itself) and R12b (the saved GAM's
moonstone bytes 0x28a..0x2a9) through a new read seam in the memory save stub.

Second pass: the same case reported build-failed -- the mutation text left a
variable unused under -Werror, so it proved nothing. The mutation was rewritten
to keep the variable; the final pass (batch53-mutation-summary.log) kills all
22 cases, words_seal_not_persisted by W7b.
